Aim: Write a program to implement Character Stuffing in a frame.
Theory:
F Character Stuffing is a ESC FLAG technique ESC ESC Nin the Data
Link Layer F computer networks to identify the beginning and end of a
frame.
In character stuffing, special characters are used to indicate the beginning and
end of a frame.
● FLAG → indicates start/end of frame.
● ESC → used before FLAG or ESC appearing in the data.
● If FLAG or ESC occurs inside the data, an ESC is inserted before it.
Program
def character_stuffing(data):
FLAG = 'F'
ESC = 'E'
stuffed_data = FLAG
for ch in data:
if ch == FLAG or ch == ESC:
stuffed_data += ESC
stuffed_data += ch
stuffed_data += FLAG
return stuffed_data
# Main program
data = input("Enter the data/frame: ")
stuffed_frame = character_stuffing(data)
print("\nOriginal Data :", data)
print("Stuffed Frame :", stuffed_frame)
Example
Enter the data/frame: ABFECD
Original Data: ABFECD
Stuffed Frame: FABEFEECD F
